Subject: Add a mingwX64 target that builds only the Kotlin half of skiko

skiko publishes no Kotlin/Native target for Windows. This adds one, with three
changes and a stub:

- build.gradle.kts declares mingwX64 behind skiko.native.mingw.enabled. It does
  not go through configureNativeTarget, because that compiles the C++ bridges
  with the target's own toolchain and embeds them with Skia into the klib. The
  bridges have to match the MSVC ABI of the prebuilt Windows Skia and the
  MinGW toolchain cannot produce that, so the klib carries Kotlin only and the
  bridges are compiled with MSVC elsewhere.
- The SymbolNameIsInternal opt-in, which was applied only when another native
  target was enabled, is applied for this one too.
- sourceHierarchy.kt puts a mingw group beside linux under native.
- Resources.native.kt: ftell returns C long, which is 32 bits on Windows and 64
  bits on every other native target, so its result is widened where it is
  read.
- SkiaLayer.mingw.kt is the same unimplemented stub Linux has. The renderer
  draws into a window of its own and never uses SkiaLayer.

---
diff --git a/skiko/build.gradle.kts b/skiko/build.gradle.kts
index 3961ddc..9f2b753 100644
--- a/skiko/build.gradle.kts
+++ b/skiko/build.gradle.kts
@@ -155,6 +155,13 @@ kotlin {
         skikoProjectContext.configureNativeTarget(OS.Linux, Arch.X64, linuxX64())
         skikoProjectContext.configureNativeTarget(OS.Linux, Arch.Arm64, linuxArm64())
     }
+    // Windows without a JVM. Only the Kotlin half is built here: the C++ half has to match
+    // the MSVC ABI of the prebuilt Skia, and the MinGW toolchain this target compiles with
+    // cannot produce that, so the bridges are compiled with MSVC separately and linked
+    // into the final executable beside Skia. Nothing is embedded into this klib.
+    if (findProperty("skiko.native.mingw.enabled") == "true") {
+        mingwX64().generateVersion(OS.Windows, Arch.X64, skiko)
+    }
     if (supportNativeIosArm64) {
         skikoProjectContext.configureNativeTarget(OS.IOS, Arch.Arm64, iosArm64())
     }
@@ -221,7 +228,7 @@ kotlin {
         implementation(kotlin("test-wasm-js"))
     }
 
-    if (supportAnyNative) {
+    if (supportAnyNative || findProperty("skiko.native.mingw.enabled") == "true") {
         sourceSets.all {
             // Really ugly, see https://youtrack.jetbrains.com/issue/KT-46649 why it is required,
             // note that setting it per source set still keeps it unset in commonized source sets.
